course: dictionary
lesson: 10694
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, the words around them, shows you which meaning the writer means. «The unruly class would not sit still.» Here unruly describes people who behave badly and are hard to control.
explain: The same word can describe something very different. «Her unruly hair stuck up in every direction.» Hair cannot behave badly, so unruly here means untidy and hard to keep neat. Ask yourself: who or what is unruly, and what is going on around it?
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. If «the unruly crowd pushed towards the gate» still makes sense when you think of "hard to control", you have it right.
fact: Unruly is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «an unruly class» or «unruly hair».
fact: Unruly means behaving badly and hard to control.
fact: Unruly hair is untidy and hard to keep neat.
fact: «High-spirited» means noisy and unruly, not keeping to the rules.
fact: Unruly can describe people, crowds and behaviour, such as unruly behaviour on planes or at football matches. Its forms are unruly, unrulier, unruliest.
exercise: «The unruly class would not sit still.» What does unruly mean here? | *Behaving badly and hard to control | Covered in paint | Lost in the woods | Very tidy and quiet
exercise: «Her unruly hair stuck up in every direction.» What does unruly mean in this sentence? | Long and curly like a wave | Shiny and clean | Behaving badly in class | *Untidy and hard to keep neat
exercise: Which word means noisy and unruly, not keeping to the rules? | Gentle | *High-spirited | Tidy | Calm
test: Which meaning fits «an unruly crowd»? | Empty and quiet | Quiet and polite | Tidy and neat | *Behaving badly and hard to control
test: Which sentence uses unruly to mean untidy? | *«Her unruly hair would not lie flat.» | «The unruly class was loud.» | «The unruly crowd cheered.» | «The unruly team argued with the referee.»
exam: Which is the best meaning of unruly in «unruly behaviour on the bus»? | Clean and shiny | Lost and alone | Kind and gentle | *Behaving badly and hard to control
